00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.180
So what are we here for today?

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:43.970
So today, we're here to
talk about fleet management

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.820
and how predictive maintenance
can support fleet management

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.730
activities, fleet optimization
activities specifically.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.350
Fleet management
solutions need to evolve.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.050
They need to move
from where they are.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.780
Currently, Fleet
Management solutions

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.570
are often reactive
visualizations

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:05.630
of the information that you
have available to yourselves.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.400
Reactive in terms
of maintenance,

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.960
but also reactive in terms
of any kind of optimization

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.700
activities as well.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.760
Today, fleet
organizations essentially

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.450
have to compete with a
number of disrupting factors

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:25.560
such as startups, other entrants
into the market, rising fuel

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.910
prices, and complex
emission base regulations.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.970
That's forcing them to
focus on efficiencies.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:35.390
And within that,
maintenance costs for fleets

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:41.560
account for 15% to 20% of
your fleet's total costs,

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:46.900
so a prime area for optimization
and a prime area for AI and IoT

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:50.230
based solutions to
help reduce that cost.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.960
Digital technologies are
changing most industries

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.760
in all areas, and
this is somewhere

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.980
where there's a
great opportunity

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:02.210
to provide efficiencies
and cost savings.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.970
Just to give you all a bit
of contextual background

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.840
information, there are a
number of fleet maintenance

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.700
optimization challenges
that need to be addressed.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.890
So Fleet Managers often lack the
pertinent asset condition data.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.260
They may have data, but
a lot of the data that

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.180
gets collected across
fleets is captured

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.880
by individuals as
opposed to necessarily

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.220
being streamed back from
the vehicles themselves

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.460
in all instances.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.120
There's excessive operational
maintenance costs,

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:34.250
so a majority of organizations
from a maintenance perspective

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.240
do periodic or cyclical
maintenance, where essentially

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.220
you are maintaining the
asset on a time based process

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.530
to essentially reduce
the risk associated

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.290
with that asset failing
at any point in time.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.350
That's due to a lack of
available asset condition data

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.050
and a limited understanding
of the relationships

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:56.840
between the asset failure
events and the data

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.672
that you can get from
those assets beforehand.

00:06:00.672 --> 00:06:02.880
Assets are becoming a whole
lot more complex as well,

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.720
so fleet operators
are having to manage

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.390
at larger scales with
more complex assets,

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:14.020
and that brings with it
its own nightmares as well.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:18.210
And there's also the
challenge around knowing

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.850
when to maintain your assets
and when to replace your assets.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:27.120
So for example, end
of life for assets

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.430
is calculated by organizations
usually on a time basis.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.250
We can bring additional
data in to help

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:38.280
those types of organizations
retire those assets

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.740
and replace those assets
when they need to not just

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.650
because a certain
time has elapsed.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.883
So this is a maturing process.

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:48.300
The move to
predictive maintenance

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.110
doesn't happen overnight.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.710
We're on this trend
moving from data

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.770
reporting through to
descriptive analytics

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.740
and dashboarding to help
people understand their assets,

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.920
and through their use of
data and bringing in data,

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.645
you're able to move to
the predictive world

00:07:04.645 --> 00:07:06.270
before we get to the
prescriptive world

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.980
where you're doing things
because you feel they're

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.810
going to fail or
you're doing things

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.760
before you need to do it.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:17.080
Moving to Predictive Maintenance
is expected to save 10% to 20%

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.270
over preventative
maintenance practices,

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.220
and we'll break that
down a little bit as we

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.080
talk through this conversation.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.400
And why now?

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.060
The big question is, has this
not been possible previously?

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.790
Why are we able to do
this at this point?

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.520
Technology convergence
is a key reason

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.630
we're able to essentially bring
a number of different data sets

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:45.540
together from both Edge devices
within vehicles, within assets,

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.218
as well as streaming data
from other data sources.

00:07:49.218 --> 00:07:50.760
So we're talking
about the map, we're

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:54.120
talking about condition
data and all those pieces,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.600
enabled by cloud computing
and big data tool kits.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:01.860
So they really allow us to
stream and store vast amount

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:05.550
of data efficiently,
economically, and securely

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:09.450
providing monitoring
capabilities and the ability

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.820
to make interventions
before issues occur.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.370
AI machine learnings
can be trained

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:19.170
against these large data set
at comparatively low cost

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:24.030
compared to in the past,
and advanced visualizations

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.950
through the use of
augmented reality

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:29.040
and also automated
dashboarding and those elements

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:32.100
can help surface the information
to the right individuals

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.780
at the right time so that they
can make those interventions as

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.280
needed.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.370
And the big question
we have to ask

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.940
is, well, why do
you do these things?

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:45.080
Why do you go through the pain
of understanding and working

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.300
through those data elements?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.130
And it's all about delivering
value for the organizations.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.930
So fleet operations
are essentially

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.600
anticipated to reduce
costs by moving

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.790
to predictive maintenance.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.660
Improve efficiency, so I'll
give you a few examples.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.980
If we look at maintenance
as it stands at the moment,

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.110
we talked about it being
done on a cyclical basis.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.700
If you maintain
assets when they need

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.430
to be maintained as opposed
to for the sake of it,

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.320
you reduce the downtime
for those assets.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.920
So for example, you don't need
to take vehicles out of service

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.350
to go and do maintenance
against those assets.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.755
You therefore make
those assets available,

00:09:23.755 --> 00:09:25.130
and you can improve
your revenues

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.930
against those at that point.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.560
You're reducing your
operational costs.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.740
You're not having individuals
having to go and service assets

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.180
that do not need to be done.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:38.430
And you also are able
to manage your Capex

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.190
and essentially focus and
work on those assets that

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.790
need the work when
they need the work.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:46.930
So I've given you
a bit of context

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:51.700
and a bit of information around
why fleet organizations need

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.540
to consider predictive
maintenance,

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.700
need to understand
their assets better.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.040
And that's understood,
and that's a key driver

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:01.670
across the industry.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:03.850
However, there are
technological challenges

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:07.660
associated with this in terms
of streaming back fleet data.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.790
So a lot of the data that
you pull off the vehicles,

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:14.830
for example, are unstructured,
or the data sources that

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.740
are available come through
as time series data

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:22.480
with varying
structures and schemas.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.080
IoT data itself isn't going
to help you generate insight.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.900
Insight comes together
from a combination

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.930
of additional
contextual data sources,

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:35.260
so knowing the actual
events that were occurring

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.030
at that point in time--

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.070
climate, temperature,
terrain, where

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.250
you were with that vehicle.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:44.070
And also within the
work we've done,

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:46.740
we've identified that
you need SME input,

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:50.100
you need the knowledge and
information from those SMEs

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.020
that are working in
that space to help you

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.290
focus on the right use cases.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.040
You can bring back
data from many sources,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.360
but unless it's actually
serving a purpose

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:01.110
and working for the use case to
help the organization deliver

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.345
value, it's not going
to be worthwhile.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:08.030
So I'll give you a bit
of an overview here

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:12.620
around what we have created
and why we have created it.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:16.700
So essentially, Hitachi
has used GCP technologies

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.160
to deliver a Predictive
Maintenance Fleet Operations

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:22.620
Solution which overcome some of
the challenges I talked about.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.190
We do two things
predominantly, and we'll

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:29.720
go into a lot of detail around
this from an actual feature

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.980
perspective and
functionality perspective.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.800
But just as a high level
overview at this point,

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.140
we have created data dashboards
for maintenance planners that

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:42.590
look at the data that we pull
out of those vehicles compared

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:46.797
to contextual data sources,
and they look at the fault

00:11:46.797 --> 00:11:48.380
information that
we've already created

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:50.470
and the AI models
we have created

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:53.180
to predict fault events.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.690
And they surface the
right recommendations

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.480
to that maintenance planner
at the right time so they know

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.990
where and when they
need to maintain assets

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.382
comparing that against the
alerts that are also coming

00:12:04.382 --> 00:12:06.340
back from the vehicle,
so it can be dynamically

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:10.090
updated throughout
their planning process,

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.940
but also looking at the
normal maintenance schedules

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:18.540
as well for those assets that
are not quite ready for this.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.090
What we've also done is
working with our client

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:25.350
around the maintenance and
inspection space as well.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.090
We've helped them
identify where they

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:31.200
need to work on their assets,
and we're using an AR guided

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:36.090
inspection application to help
their largely mobile workforce

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:39.000
understand the steps
they need to take

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.370
to complete that inspection
against that vehicle.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:43.860
So our client has a
large mobile workforce,

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.950
but they also have a large
number of contractors

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.920
that they use as well.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:51.800
And the AR guarded
application has

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:56.390
been super useful to helping
those contractor workforce

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:58.970
individuals understand
what they need to do

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.530
and where they need to do it.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.580
We'll give you a
demonstration of that as well.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:06.820
So that is using the AR
components of Android

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:11.280
but also using
Google Glass as well.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.875
So in terms of giving you the
